```

Open the serial terminal with:

```bash
gtkterm -p /dev/ttyS0 -s 115200
```

## Implemented Commands

### Train Speed

```text
tr <train> <speed>
```

The user-facing speed range is `0..120`, matching the CS3 speed scale.

Examples:

```text
tr 14 20
tr 14 60
tr 14 100
tr 14 0
```

`tr 14 0` stops the train.

### Switch Control

```text
sw <switch> <S|C>
```

Examples:

```text
sw 2 S
sw 2 C
```

### Route Setup

```text
route <target>
```

Example:

```text
route C8
```

This sets the switches required for the selected target.

### Stop Plan Preview

```text
plan <target> <speed>
```

Example:

```text
plan C8 30
```

This previews the route/stop plan without moving the train.

### Automatic Stop

```text
stop <train> <target> <speed>
```

Example:

```text
stop 14 C8 30
```

This command sets the route, starts the train, waits for the predicted run time, and then sends speed 0 to stop the train.

### Demo

```text
demo
```

Runs the default route/stop demonstration.

### Calibration / Observation

```text
cal
targets
obs <target> <speed> <ticks>
status
```

`obs` compares an observed run time against the current prediction model. It does not move the train.

The TC1 calibration image keeps `IdleTask` silent so periodic diagnostic text
cannot interleave with command acknowledgements or timestamped observations.

## Implementation Notes

Train commands are sent through the MCP2515 CAN controller.

For the tested Track D setup, train 14 is controlled as MM address 14 using the locomotive speed CAN frame:

```text
CAN ID: 0x00085772
DATA:   00 00 00 0E <speed_hi> <speed_lo>
```

The user-facing speed `0..120` is converted to a 10-bit Märklin speed value `0..1000`.

The MCP2515 initialization was made more robust by explicitly entering configuration mode, writing the timing/configuration registers, and waiting for normal mode before sending CAN frames.

For TC1, CAN sending is synchronous so terminal commands do not block indefinitely on the old asynchronous queue path.

## Tested Commands

The following were tested successfully on Track D with train 14:

```text
tr 14 20
tr 14 60
tr 14 100
tr 14 0
sw 2 S
sw 2 C
route C8
plan C8 30
stop 14 C8 30
```

